Teton Song Highway summit coordinates and GeoNames elevation values in
tools/build-teton-tour.mjs are derived from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/),
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

The ten entries were selected from the repository's ridgeview/data/peaks.json
snapshot. Teewinot Mountain is labelled Teewinot to match the implementation
plan. Published elevation checks are stored separately from GeoNames values.

tools/build-tour-names.mjs selects summit, lake, pass and valley features
from the GeoNames US dump under the same CC BY 4.0 license, transforms their
coordinates into the tour's local metric frame, and records the input hash.

View Scout's geographic camera leads are derived from the repository's
Ridgeview snapshot (GeoNames names, CC BY 4.0, and Wikidata names, CC0).
Its coarse terrain previews use Terrain Tiles on AWS, provided by Mapzen /
Tilezen, with USGS 3DEP, SRTM, GMTED and ETOPO sources by region and zoom.
Dataset: https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
Source attribution: https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md
Previews are reduced-resolution derived images for composition discovery;
they do not reproduce the production terrain, materials or water treatment.

Song range pilot stages (src/assets/range/v2/terrain/song-range-pilot-*.terrain.*,
built by tools/build-song-range-pilot.mjs) are composed from massifs cut out of
USGS 3D Elevation Program 1/3 arc-second DEMs (public domain, U.S. Government
work; credit U.S. Geological Survey) around the Teton Range, Wyoming; the
Sawtooth Range, Idaho; the Sneffels Range, Colorado; and Crater Lake, Oregon.
Massif relief above each piece's base is measured DEM; the lake and land floor
between pieces is generated. Each stage's build record lists its source tiles,
window hashes and pieces.
